stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> queued: Git commit and tracking row recorded
  queued --> building: Matching run is in progress
  queued --> live: Matching run succeeded
  building --> live: Matching run succeeded
  queued --> failed: Confirmed failure or absence timeout
  building --> failed: Confirmed unsuccessful run or absence timeout
  state "live (terminal)" as live
  state "failed (terminal)" as failed

  note right of queued
    Unavailable lookup: retain last state.
    Confirmed absence can fail after 10 minutes.
    Source SHA, branch and workflow must match.
  end note
  note right of live
    Live-kind: workflow reports live deployment.
    Preview-kind: preview ready.
    Verify the edited page separately.
  end note
  note right of failed
    Failure can follow partial S3 writes.
    Retry handoff or identity can also fail.
    Eligible retry creates a new tracking row.
    Terminal records do not reopen.
  end note
